<title>USA: Dow Chemical Texas plant has small release.</title>
<headline>Dow Chemical Texas plant has small release.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dow Chemical Co's La Porte, Texas plant accidentally released hydrochloric acid gas early Tuesday, though the leak was quickly sealed and no injuries or threat to the community was seen, a plant spokesman said.</p>
<p>The leak, which took place at 0551 CST/1051 GMT, was halted in about an hour by plant personnel, the spokesman said. The plant produces isocyanates for use in automotive applications and insulation.</p>
<p>((--Matt Daily, New York Energy Desk +1 212 859 1620))</p>
